<title>DENMARK: SAS plummets into major 1997 Q1 loss.</title>
<headline>SAS plummets into major 1997 Q1 loss.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31 1997</p>
<p>				(million Swedish crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net turnover	     8,354   vs  8,206</p>
<p> Group pre-tax result	 minus 269 vs  plus 311</p>
<p> Group operating result     minus 247 vs  plus 309</p>
<p> Operating costs	    minus 8,175  vs   minus 7,567</p>
<p>Group operating result before</p>
<p> depreciation			   179  vs 639</p>
<p> Net financial items	  minus 22   vs   plus 2</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of jointly owned Swedish-Danish-Norwegian airline group is Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS). It said in a statement that it expected a full year 1997 pre-tax profit similar to 1996's 1.815 billion Swedish crowns. The result was significantly below analyst expectations.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969652</p>
